## §1.7 prose update check (NON-ACTION — verified clean at S2 authoring time)

A natural worry on applying this diff is whether the two excluded rules' own §1.7
self-reflexive notes name "always-on CLAUDE.md injection" as a delivery channel that would
now be stale. Verified at proposal authoring time (2026-07-30):

- `.claude/rules/autonomous-loop-continuity.md §5` — its §1.7 forward-check names
  "Stop hook" + "always-on autonomy block in `inject-session-bootstrap.sh`" as the channels.
  Always-on CLAUDE.md injection is NOT named. No prose update needed.
- `.claude/rules/git-conflict-merge-forward.md §6/§7` — its forward-check names
  "`~/.claude/hooks/git-safety.sh` (operator-global PreToolUse hook)" + "the always-on
  CLAUDE.md `Harness gates` pointer bullet". The CLAUDE.md pointer stays in CLAUDE.md (it is
  a one-line bullet in `### Harness gates`, not the rule file); the rule file itself was
  never named as the channel. No prose update needed.

If you are reading this proposal at a later date and either rule's §1.7 has been amended to
claim always-on CLAUDE.md injection as a channel, re-verify and update the rule's §1.7 prose
in the same maintainer commit. As of commit 336d031ef there is nothing to update.

## Why this is safe

- **`autonomous-loop-continuity.md` — proposal 2 compensates.** The rule's own Class header
  (`:9`) declares its channels as (a) Stop-hook arm + (b) autonomy block in
  `inject-session-bootstrap.sh`. Always-on CLAUDE.md injection was never a declared channel;
  removing it aligns runtime with the declared contract (the failure mode Note B exists to
  prevent — declaring a channel that doesn't fire is the dual failure).
- **`git-conflict-merge-forward.md` — accepted degradation.** Note C records the cost (one
  wasted first-attempt cycle for an agent meeting a CONFLICTING PR) and the mitigation (the
  operator-global `git-safety.sh` blocks `git rebase` at execution time, and the CLAUDE.md
  Harness-gates pointer bullet still routes to the recipe). 9,285 bytes saved per
  session-start in exchange for that cost.

## Risks if misapplied

- **Applying without proposal 2** strands §2 for every session. Rejected by step 0 of the
  apply recipe above.
- **Adding extra entries** (e.g. copying `egress-no-api-bypass.md` twice) silently breaks
  other invariants — `claudeMdExcludes` is a flat array, no schema enforcement beyond JSON
  validity. Use `jq` to verify the post-apply array contents.
- **Including a non-existent file** is a silent no-op (CC's loader just skips it). Both new
  entries are verified-existent at S1: `ls .claude/rules/autonomous-loop-continuity.md
  .claude/rules/git-conflict-merge-forward.md` → both present.
